GH issue: https://github.com/clankercode/lsp-openplanet/issues/55 (gh-55)

Verified still open 2026-08-24 @ 728c30d: `src/analysis/unused.rs:142` — "Locals and
parameters are deliberately out of scope (deferred)". Probe (`/tmp/probe55`) with an
unused local + unused param emits no local/param warning.

## Scope
Local-scope usage pass over function bodies: unused local variables and unused
function/method parameters. Reuses `Checker::define_local`/`lookup_local` +
`with_usage_recording`.

## DECISIONS (do not re-litigate; rationale inline)

1. **Read-vs-write**: warn only when the identifier is never *mentioned again*
   anywhere after its declaration in the enclosing scope. A write-only local
   (`x = 1;` with no read) counts as USED. Rationale: FP-hostile repo culture
   (todo-false-positives.txt); dead-store analysis needs real flow analysis and
   would misfire on `&out` params, loop accumulators, and `cast<>` temporaries.
2. **Param cascade**: params warn only when the enclosing function is itself
   *used* (an unused function already warns at the declaration level — no
   double-warn). Params of declarations without bodies (imports, funcdefs,
   interface methods, abstract/mixin decls) never warn.
3. **Signature-fixed params never warn**: params of Openplanet callbacks
   (`OPENPLANET_CALLBACKS` + the gh-56 config list), operator overloads, virtual
   overrides / interface implementations, and functions in public-API export
   files. Their signature is imposed by the caller, not chosen by the author.
4. **Suppression**: same conventions as the file-level pass — leading `_` on the
   identifier and trailing `// lsp: ignore unused` on the declaration line.
5. **Loop/catch/for-init locals**: `for (uint i = 0; ...)` counts the condition
   and increment as usage (they are in the same scope). A loop var never
   mentioned outside the init still warns.
6. **Enablement gate**: dogfood against `tests/fixtures/tm-*` (E++, dips++)
   BEFORE flipping the default. Zero new FPs → default on. Any FP that is not
   cleanly exemptable → ship behind config key `unused_locals` (top-level in
   `.openplanet-lsp.toml`, tri-state like `warnings_as_errors`) defaulting to
   FALSE, and record the FP in todo-false-positives.txt. Report which path was
   taken.
7. **Message wording** mirrors the existing pass: "a local variable `x` is never
   used (suppress with a leading `_` or a trailing `// lsp: ignore unused`
   comment)" / "a parameter `p` is never used (...)".

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Generalized variants per AGENTS.md: unused local; used local; write-only local;
`_`-prefixed; `// lsp: ignore unused`; shadowed local in nested block; loop var;
param unused in used function (warns); param unused in unused function (single
warn at decl only); `const T &in` / `T &out` / `T &` / `T@` / `T@ &in` param
variants; callback param; override param; operator-overload param; method params
on a used vs unused class; exports-file function params.

## Lane
Lane A, step 1 of 2. Landing this first shrinks gh-56 (the exemption list gets a
second consumer: params). Files: src/analysis/unused.rs, src/typecheck/checker.rs
(locals usage recording), src/server/diagnostics.rs (message plumbing if needed),
tests/.